autodoc.datatype  (c) 2026 Amiga Developer

Desc: A MorphOS/AROS/AmigaOS Datatype for viewing Amiga Autodoc
      documentation files with formatted rendering.

Format: autodoc documentation, per the AmigaOS Autodoc Style Guide.
        Files: *.autodoc, *.doc (mapped by the Autodoc descriptor that
        make builds and installs to DEVS:DataTypes).

Credits:
  - AmigaOS Documentation Wiki, "Autodoc Style Guide":
        https://wiki.amigaos.net/wiki/Autodoc_Style_Guide
        Copyright (c) Hyperion Entertainment and contributors.
  - Structure modeled after the AROS ascii.datatype:
        Copyright (c) 1995-2001, The AROS Development Team.
        www.morphos-team.net/files/src/3.20/ascii.datatype.tar.bz2
  - See also markdown.datatype (creep-ltx's AmigaDatatypes), the
        descriptor tool here (tools/mkdesc.py) is adapted from it, MIT:
        https://github.com/creep-ltx/AmigaDatatypes

Features:
  - Renders Autodoc blocks with bold section headings.
  - Strips "/****** ... ***" block decorations.
  - Supports internal (/****i* ) and obsolete (/****o* ) markers.
  - Recognizes NAME, SYNOPSIS, FUNCTION, INPUTS, RESULT, EXAMPLE,
    NOTES, BUGS, SEE ALSO sections.
  - Tabulator size honors the TABSIZE environment variable.
  - Ignores form feed (0x0C) page separators.

Installation:
  Place autodoc.datatype in SYS:Classes/Datatypes (AmigaOS/AROS) or
  SYS:MorphOS/classes/datatypes (MorphOS), and the Autodoc descriptor
  in DEVS:DataTypes ('make install' does both copies), then either
  reboot or run:
      AddDataTypes autodoc.datatype
      AddDataTypes REFRESH
  or use the OS-specific datatype flush utility.

Copy/quad note:
  This is a template datatype implementation. Adapt the header comment
  to your project and run 'make bump' before release.